Third-party notices
===================

rhci itself is MIT-licensed (see LICENSE). Some of its files are derived
from other projects, whose licences apply to those parts:

  prelude/Prelude.hs
      Ported from GHC's base library (base-4.18, shipped with GHC 9.6),
      with GHC's definitions wherever behaviour is observable.
      Licence: base's licence, below (BSD-style; includes the Haskell
      Report's notice).

  prelude/Data/Map/Internal.hs, prelude/Data/Map/Strict/Internal.hs,
  prelude/Data/Set/Internal.hs
      Ported from the containers package (containers-0.6.7).
      Licence: containers' licence, below (BSD-3-Clause).

  lib/rhci/unicode_data.rb, oracle/unicode/tables.txt
      Generated from GHC's Unicode tables (dumped by oracle/unicode/Tables.hs),
      which derive from the Unicode Character Database.
      Licence: Unicode License v3, below.

The standalone rhci binaries also contain mruby, which is not part of
this repository (vendor/ is fetched at build time), and the release
builds a C library:

  rhci (the portable executable, `rake cosmo`)
      Cosmopolitan Libc, licence: ISC, below. Cosmopolitan bundles
      further components (parts of musl, FreeBSD and OpenBSD, zlib, TRE,
      ...) under permissive licences; it embeds each one's notice in the
      binary itself, so `strings rhci | grep -B1 -A2 Copyright` lists
      exactly what a given binary contains.

  rhci-linux-x86_64-musl (`rake musl`)
      musl libc, licence: MIT, below (with the notices of the code musl
      itself incorporates).

Distributions of a binary must include the notices for what it contains:
mruby's, and the libc's.


